      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "In FY2024, the Union of Concerned Scientists spent <cite id=\"1\">87.0% of its budget directly on program activities</cite>, exceeding the standard 75% sector benchmark for financial efficiency [1]. Its operations are backed by strong reserve management, holding <cite id=\"1\">15.0 months of working capital</cite> to ensure financial stability during multi-year policy initiatives [1]. Third-party evaluators confirm these operational practices, resulting in an <cite id=\"1\">overall rating of 97.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite> [1]. Furthermore, the organization published technical research identifying <cite id=\"3\">a $4.3 billion transmission cost issue</cite> in regional power markets, illustrating how technical research supports public policy outcomes [3]."
      ],
      "summary": "The Union of Concerned Scientists works to advance clean energy, climate resilience, and global security through technical research and public policy advocacy [6]. Operating as an established advocacy and research organization, it uses scientific analysis to influence power grid regulations and national security policies [6]. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"2\">Total Revenue of $41,916,878</cite>, demonstrating significant operational scope in science-based advocacy [2]. The group maintains a strong financial standing, holding <cite id=\"1\">a 97/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite> alongside <cite id=\"1\">15.0 months of working capital in working capital</cite> [1]. While the organization excels in administrative efficiency and research output, its focus remains strictly on policy reform and technical capacity building rather than direct humanitarian aid [6]. Furthermore, as a non-faith-based policy group, donations support general advocacy.",
